{"title":"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2020 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Annie (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />), Bogdan (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />), Cao (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />), Daniel (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />), and Emily (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />) are running for student government positions. Their campaign posters are printed by different printing companies. The graph below plots each student’s total price of their first batch of posters versus the number of posters in their first batch.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>(put graph on problem 1 page)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Daniel pays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f8f539c1b3a2c8df6aa0be01f15ec1342734b1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$16.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> posters which is a price of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c030e1eabde01498527b3c53e08763522c0c7da2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$1.60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> per poster. What does Cao pay for poster?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the problem, point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> represents the number of posters that Cao makes, as well as the total price.\n</p><p>From the graph, we can see that Cao pays <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/c/66c9188bf653d75c3d3a270275c8fe619157370b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$7.00$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> in total for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> posters. This would be:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/2/0f20e790279ce5c216b6bcaea7db5a0860f7e2e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\$7.00}{14 \\text{ posters}} = \\boxed {\\$0.50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"158\" height=\"44\" /> per poster\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018012716\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.021 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 58/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1259/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2122/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.290      1 2020_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%   13.290      1 -total\n 38.56%    5.124      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35550:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018012716 and revision id 277896. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}